---
// The home page: what paros is now (the consensus core and its proofs), the
// Paxos flavors to learn, and the journal designed on top of them.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Panel from "../components/Panel.astro";
import { REPO, url } from "../nav";
const TAG = `${REPO}/tree/v0.2.0-alpha.1`;
---
<Base>
  <div class="home">
    <div class="titleblock hero">
      <div class="kicker label">paros · Paxos in Rust</div>
      <h1>The Paxos family, built from the ground up</h1>
      <p class="lede">paros builds Paxos one flavor at a time: single decree, Multi-Paxos,
        matchmakers, grid quorums, proxy leaders and replicas. Each flavor is a sans-IO state
        machine, and each gets a TLA+ model before anything is built on it. You can step through
        every one of them in your browser, on the code paros ships.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href={url("paxos/tour/")}>▶ Learn the Paxos flavors</a>
        <a class="btn" href={url("consensus/")}>How it is built</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="strip" aria-label="paros in figures">
      <div><span class="k">Paxos flavors</span><span class="v">5</span></div>
      <div><span class="k">I/O in the core</span><span class="v">none</span></div>
      <div><span class="k">Before code</span><span class="v">TLA+</span></div>
    </div>

    <Panel num="01" title="Learn the flavors">
      <ol class="index-list">
        <li><a href={url("paxos/single-decree/")}>Single-decree Paxos</a><span class="desc">Two phases choose one value, once.</span></li>
        <li><a href={url("paxos/multi-paxos/")}>Multi-Paxos</a><span class="desc">A log of slots with a stable leader.</span></li>
        <li><a href={url("paxos/matchmaker/")}>Matchmaker Paxos</a><span class="desc">Change the acceptors with no stop.</span></li>
        <li><a href={url("paxos/compartmentalized/")}>Compartmentalized Paxos</a><span class="desc">Split the leader into roles that scale alone.</span></li>
        <li><a href={url("paxos/quorums/")}>Quorums</a><span class="desc">Majority, grid and partitions: who must answer.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </Panel>

    <Panel num="02" title="The core" meta="paros-consensus">
      <ul class="caps">
        <li><b>Sans-IO</b><span><code>paros-consensus</code> has no I/O, no clock and no randomness. Inputs go in, one <code>Ready</code> comes out, and the driver does the I/O in a fixed order.</span></li>
        <li><b>One role per file</b><span>Proposer, acceptor, replica, matchmaker, proxy leader, batcher, quorum read: the roles of the papers, composed into deployments.</span></li>
        <li><b>Models first</b><span>A rule that the papers do not have, or a flavor that is not modelled yet, gets a TLA+ model and a control before its code.</span></li>
        <li><b>Eleven examples</b><span>Small runnable programs drive the deployments and the roles, and assert the property each one shows.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="aside"><a href={url("consensus/")}>The library</a> · <a href={url("consensus/driver/")}>the driver loop</a> · <a href={url("consensus/deployments/")}>the deployments</a> · <a href={url("consensus/proof/")}>how it is checked</a></p>
    </Panel>

    <Panel num="03" title="The journal" meta="to be designed again">
      <p>One ordered, durable log for each journal id, with four calls: <code>Write</code>, <code>Read</code>, <code>Truncate</code> and <code>SetLeader</code>.
        The journal is built again on the consensus core, once the core has segments: a segment
        ends at a decided command, and the acceptors keep one log.</p>
      <p class="aside">The first design of the journal is at the tag <code>journal-design-a</code>. The service around it, <a href={url("parosd/")}><code>parosd</code></a>, is being rebuilt; the version before the
        rewrite is at the tag <a href={TAG}><code>v0.2.0-alpha.1</code></a>.</p>
    </Panel>
  </div>
</Base>
